title: "SeaExplorerIO.jl: pure-Julia readers for Alseamar SeaExplorer glider log files"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gong
    given-names: Donglai
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1697-1739"
version: 0.3.1
date-released: "2026-07-13"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21345323
repository-code: "https://github.com/oceansensing/SeaExplorerIO.jl"
keywords:
  - oceanography
  - underwater glider
  - SeaExplorer
  - glider data
  - data readers
  - Julia
abstract: >-
  SeaExplorerIO.jl reads Alseamar SeaExplorer glider log files — navigation
  (gli) and payload (pld1, legato, ...) streams, both segment-numbered logs
  from the glider computer and concatenated GLIMPSE-server CSV exports — into
  a uniform column table. It is deliberately the file layer only: stream
  discovery, transfer-gap detection, robust parsing (corrupt files skipped
  loudly, sentinel fills handled), timestamp and NMEA-coordinate
  normalization, and multi-download-route merging with exact-timestamp
  deduplication. It serves as the shared loading layer for GliderADCP.jl and
  GliderTurbulence.jl.
